  "title": "Kamehameha's conquest of Oʻahu (1795)",
  "summary": "In 1795 Kamehameha I, chief of Hawaiʻi island, took Maui and Molokaʻi, landed on Oʻahu at Waiʻalae and Waikīkī and defeated Kalanikupule in the Battle of Nuʻuanu, where defenders were driven over the Pali cliffs. He then controlled all islands except Kauaʻi, which stayed independent.",
